+# Implementation Complete: Competitive Programming Constraint-Aware Workflow
+
+## Summary
+The coding agent has been successfully updated to implement a rigorous, multi-phase constraint-aware verification workflow for competitive programming problems. The system ensures both correctness and performance verification before submission.
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+### 1. ✅ Modified `coding_agent.py` forward() Method
+**Location**: `/dgm/coding_agent.py`, lines 140-214
+
+The `forward()` method now contains a comprehensive, phased instruction set with:
+
+#### Phase 1: Constraint and Complexity Analysis (MANDATORY)
+- Requires creation of `notes.md` with:
+  - All explicit constraints (N, T, value ranges, time/memory limits)
+  - Allowed operation budget (~1e8-2e8 for Python)
+  - Chosen algorithm with complexity proof
+  - Critical bans against over-budget approaches
+- Detects over-budget algorithms BEFORE coding
+
+#### Phase 2: Brute-Force Reference and Exploration
+- `brute.py`: Simple, obviously-correct reference implementation
+- `gen.py`: Random test case generator with edge cases
+- Manual exploration to derive patterns and insights
+
+#### Phase 3: Main Solution Implementation and Sample Testing
+- `solution.py`: Fast, efficient main solution
+- Sample extraction from problem statement
+- `sample_N.txt` and `sample_N_expected.txt` for each sample
+- Automated testing with `timeout` and `diff` verification
+- No samples pass verification block
+
+#### Phase 4: Stress Testing with Random Cases
+- Uses `run_tests` tool for differential testing
+- 100 random test cases by default
+- Supports custom `checker.py` for multiple valid outputs
+- Early exit on failure with error details
+
+#### Phase 5: Max-Size Input and Timing Verification
+- Generates `max_input.txt` with worst-case constraints
+- 15-second timeout (3x the default test timeout)
+- Explicit TLE detection and flagging
+- Forces algorithm redesign instead of micro-optimization
+
+#### Phase 6: Iterate Until Complete
+- Bounded iteration (no `while True` loops)
+- Clear success criteria:
+  - All samples pass (verified with diffs)
+  - All 100 random tests pass
+  - Max-size input completes within acceptable time
+- Explicit failure modes guide debugging
+
+**Key Properties**:
+- ✅ No `while True` loops - uses bounded phases 1-6
+- ✅ Explicit tool usage instructions
+- ✅ Detailed step-by-step guidance
+- ✅ Error handling and recovery paths
+- ✅ Performance verification integrated into workflow
+
+### 2. ✅ Enhanced `tools/run_tests.py`
+**Location**: `/dgm/tools/run_tests.py`
+
+#### tool_info() Function (Lines 9-50)
+Returns proper JSON schema with:
+- `name`: "run_tests"
+- `description`: Clear explanation of functionality
+- `input_schema`: Properly structured JSON schema
+
+#### Input Schema Structure (VALIDATED)
+```json
+{
+  "type": "object",
+  "properties": {
+    "solution_path": { "type": "string", "description": "..." },
+    "brute_path": { "type": "string", "description": "..." },
+    "generator_path": { "type": "string", "description": "..." },
+    "checker_path": { "type": "string", "description": "..." },
+    "num_iterations": { "type": "integer", "description": "..." },
+    "timeout_sec": { "type": "number", "description": "..." },
+    "max_input_path": { "type": "string", "description": "..." }
+  },
+  "required": ["solution_path", "brute_path", "generator_path"]
+}
+```
+
+**Schema Validation Checklist**:
+- ✅ "type" at top level with value "object"
+- ✅ "properties" at top level with all parameter definitions
+- ✅ "required" at SAME LEVEL as "type" and "properties" (NOT nested inside properties)
+- ✅ Every property has both "type" and "description" fields
+- ✅ Required array contains exactly the three mandatory parameters
+- ✅ Optional parameters (checker_path, num_iterations, timeout_sec, max_input_path) properly omitted from required array
+
+#### tool_function() Implementation (Lines 53-206)
+
+**Differential Testing** (Lines 84-174):
+- Generates test cases with generator (timeout: default 5s)
+- Runs solution with timing (timeout: configurable)
+- Runs brute-force reference with timing (timeout: configurable)
+- Compares outputs:
+  - Via exact match (default)
+  - Via custom checker if provided
+- Returns first failure with:
+  - Input that caused failure
+  - Expected output (from brute)
+  - Actual output (from solution)
+  - Timing information
+- Handles timeouts with explicit TLE message
+- Comprehensive error reporting
+
+**Max-Size Input Testing** (Lines 176-202):
+- Reads max_input.txt if provided
+- Runs solution with 3x timeout (default 15 seconds)
+- Reports runtime or explicit TLE
+- Includes in final success message
+- Non-blocking (doesn't fail entire run, but reports it)
+
+**Return Values**:
+- Success: "All N random tests passed! [Max input test...]"
+- Failure: First failing case with full details
+- Error: Specific error messages with context
